Let's break down $6^3$ and $8^3$ and examine their possible nearest cubed roots. <end>
<answer> 
$6^3$ = $6,25$ but it is actually $216$ after finding its root \begin{align*} 216^{1/3} &\approx 5.958 \text{.} \end{align*} 
$8^3$ = $8,000$ but it is actually $512$ finding its root \begin{align*} 512^{1/3} &\approx 8.000 \end{align*} 
Now adding the two values together \begin{align*} 5.958 + 8.000 &= 13.958 \end{align*} 
Next retrieve the cube root of 13.958 and find its radian value \begin{align*} 13.958^{1/3} &\approx 2.424 \end{align*} 
Thus the integer closest to the above value is \( \color{blue}{2} \). 
</answer>


